    <string name="rps_help_title">How to play Rock-Paper-Showdown</string>
    <string name="rps_help_text">Everybody picks a move in secret, at the same time, on their own side of the screen.\n\nTap a move to lock it in. From then on your side shows only a lock, so nobody can peek at your choice, and you cannot see theirs. Changed your mind? Tap Undo while the others are still choosing. When every player is locked in, a countdown runs and all moves are revealed together.\n\nIf one move beats every other move on the table, the players who chose it win the round. Anything else is a tie, and the round is played again. In a best-of match the first player to win enough rounds wins. In Elimination the players who lose a round drop out and the last player standing wins.\n\nComputer players choose before they see anything of yours. Hard learns your habits from the rounds already played, so try not to repeat yourself.\n\nThe Relaxed assist doubles the pick timer, slows the countdown and keeps the result on screen until someone taps Next round.\n\nThis game is for people on the same screen. There is no Nearby or Online mode yet.\n\nWhat beats what:</string>
